    "text": "The points of intersection of the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. The image of the circle with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;as a diameter in the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is :",
